# um-texts 1
=== allod gipat
Gipath
Gipath is a desolate land belonging to no country. It is populated mainly by Goblins, Orcs and other creatures hostile to humans. The only human settlement is very small and under constant threat of attack.

=== allod ingos
Ingos
Ingos is part of the Canian Empire. Its territory, however, is quite large and thinly populated, so tribes of other races still inhabit this land. Ingos is divided into several provinces, each of which is ruled by a governor, who, in turn, is supported by guards assigned from the capital city. Ingos' residents still enjoy considerable freedom, though. They are very independent and not at all famous for their willingness to comply with authorities.

=== allod suslanger
Suslanger
Suslanger belongs to the Khadaganian empire. Suslanger's territory is not particularly large, and the lands suitable for living and farming are even smaller. The river which dug a deep canyon flows into the lake; it is really the only significant source of water. To extend the farming lands, people have to build dams and irrigation canals. Khadaganian authorities are cruel and ruthless. Numerous guards punish for even the smallest deviation from Emperor's decrees, while spies and eavesdroppers report on every suspicious person.

